    "section": "General English",
    "topic": "Reading Comprehension",
    "passage": "The rapid acceleration of India's retail payments architecture post-2016 catalyzed an unprecedented surge in digital transaction adoption. What was once the exclusive domain of physical cash and branch visits rapidly migrated towards mobile point-of-sale applications, digital prepaid wallets, and the Unified Payments Interface (UPI). By abstracting intricate 16-digit card credentials and bank account numbers into simple Virtual Payment Addresses (VPAs) and QR codes, payment service providers dramatically lowered customer acquisition friction. For millions of unbanked and underbanked citizens, mobile-based financial interfaces served as their maiden on-ramp to formal institutional banking.\n\nYet, this breakneck digital democratization spawned formidable operational vulnerabilities. As transaction volumes expanded exponentially, cybersecurity threat vectors migrated from sophisticated server-side penetration towards insidious social engineering attacks. Vishing, fake customer support handles on social media, fraudulent merchant QR sticker overlays, and unauthorized screen-sharing applications accounted for the overwhelming majority of retail fraud incidents in 2018. Vulnerable users, often functionally semi-literate in digital security protocols, were easily manipulated into divulging One-Time Passwords (OTPs) and UPI PINs under false pretenses of KYC compliance or prize disbursements.\n\nThe regulatory response was swift and multi-pronged. The Reserve Bank of India mandated that banks and payment system operators establish zero-liability frameworks for customers in instances of third-party fraud reported within three days, placing the fiduciary onus firmly on financial intermediaries to harden their risk mitigation perimeters. Concurrently, guidelines requiring two-factor authentication (2FA) for all domestic card-not-present transactions and end-to-end encryption of mobile payment switches demonstrated that consumer trust remains the bedrock upon which any cashless economic transformation must securely rest.",
