    "passage": null,
    "qText": "Identify the part containing a grammatical error:\nThe internal audit team discovered (A) / that the total amount of bad debts (B) / were considerably higher than (C) / what was initially estimated. (D) / No error (E)",
    "options": [
      "(A)",
      "(B)",
      "(C)",
      "(D)",
      "(E) No error"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "The head noun of the subject is 'the total amount' (singular). Therefore, the verb must be singular 'was considerably higher', not 'were'. Part (C) is erroneous.",
    "source_ref": "SBI Clerk Mains 2018 Solved Paper (Notification CRPD/CR/2017-18/10)",
    "source_url": "https://www.bankersadda.com/sbi-clerk-mains-previous-year-paper/"
