    "section": "Quantitative Aptitude",
    "topic": "Arithmetic",
    "passage": null,
    "qText": "In a 75-liter mixture of milk and water, the ratio of milk to water is 4 : 1. How much water must be added to make the ratio of milk to water 3 : 2?",
    "options": [
      "15 liters",
      "20 liters",
      "25 liters",
      "30 liters",
      "35 liters"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "Milk = (4/5) \u00d7 75 = 60 liters. Water = 15 liters. In new ratio 3:2, milk remains 60 liters => 3 parts = 60 => 1 part = 20. Water required = 2 \u00d7 20 = 40 liters. Water to be added = 40 - 15 = 25 liters.",
    "source_ref": "SBI Clerk Mains 2019 Solved Paper (Notification CRPD/CR/2019-20/03)",
    "source_url": "https://www.bankersadda.com/sbi-clerk-mains-previous-year-paper/"
