    "section": "General English",
    "topic": "Reading Comprehension",
    "passage": "The year 2022 witnessed the abrupt unwinding of a decade-long macroeconomic regime defined by near-zero interest rates and quantitative easing. As synchronized pandemic stimulus collided with acute supply bottlenecks and sudden geopolitical conflagrations in Eastern Europe, global commodity and energy markets were roiled by inflationary shocks not witnessed since the 1970s. In response, the world's preeminent central banks executed their most aggressive coordinated tightening campaign in four decades. The rapid escalating of policy rates by the US Federal Reserve catalyzed an aggressive appreciation of the US dollar, which in turn transmitted inflationary pressures across import-dependent emerging market economies through higher landed costs for crude oil, fertilizer, and strategic raw materials.\n\nFor developing nations, this 'dollar smile' dynamic imposed severe balance-of-payments strain. Sovereign debt servicing burdens surged, foreign portfolio investors repatriated capital to safe-haven assets, and domestic currencies experienced unprecedented downward depreciation. Yet, the Indian economy exhibited notable structural fortitude amidst this turbulent external environment. A well-capitalized banking system, moderate external commercial debt, and substantial foreign exchange reserves enabled the Reserve Bank of India to manage volatility without resorting to disruptive capital controls. Nevertheless, the protracted conflict and tightening financial conditions have underscored the acute necessity of domestic supply chain resilience, strategic energy diversification, and fiscal prudence to navigate the emerging paradigm of global geoeconomic fragmentation.",
