    "passage": null,
    "qText": "Identify the segment containing a grammatical error:\nScarcely had the statutory auditor (A) / entered the bank vault (B) / than the security alarm sounded (C) / triggering a complete branch lockdown. (D) / No error (E)",
    "options": [
      "Scarcely had the statutory auditor",
      "entered the bank vault",
      "than the security alarm sounded",
      "triggering a complete branch lockdown",
      "No error"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "Correlative conjunction rule: 'Scarcely... when' is the correct pair, not 'scarcely... than' (which is used with 'No sooner... than'). It should be 'when the security alarm sounded'.",
    "source_ref": "SBI Clerk Mains 2022 Solved Paper (Notification CRPD/CR/2022-23/15)",
