    "correctAnswer": 4,
    "explanation": "For I: (x - 6)(x - 8) = 0 => x = 6, 8.\nFor II: (y - 8)(y - 10) = 0 => y = 8, 10.\nWhen x = 8 and y = 8, x = y. When x = 6 and y = 8, x < y. But if x = 8 and y = 8, x=y; if x=8 and y=10, x<y. However x is never greater than y, so x \u2264 y.",
