    "topic": "Reading Comprehension",
    "passage": "The meteoric proliferation of generative artificial intelligence and large foundation models has precipitated a profound transformation across retail financial services. Autonomous algorithms now synthesize massive unstructured datasets, automate algorithmic credit appraisals, and power conversational virtual assistants capable of sophisticated natural language engagement. In commercial banking, cognitive systems have dramatically compressed loan turnaround times, democratized micro-credit evaluation for informal gig workers lacking traditional credit bureau histories, and augmented real-time anti-money laundering vigilance. Yet, this rapid technological mainstreaming introduces formidable ethical, regulatory, and systemic risks.\n\nParamount among these vulnerabilities is algorithmic opacity, colloquially termed the 'black box' conundrum. Deep neural networks frequently derive creditworthiness and interest rate determinations through complex probabilistic interactions that defy human interpretability. Historical datasets imbued with socioeconomic prejudice risk codifying and exacerbating systemic credit rationing against marginalized demographics. Furthermore, generative AI democratizes malevolent hacking vectors: hyper-realistic synthetic voice clones and synthetic deepfake videos now readily bypass conventional biometric voice and video KYC authentication firewalls. In response, global regulatory authorities and the RBI have intensified oversight, mandating model explainability, algorithmic audits, robust human-in-the-loop safeguards, and stringent adherence to the Digital Personal Data Protection legal framework.",
