    "section": "Quantitative Aptitude",
    "topic": "Arithmetic",
    "passage": null,
    "qText": "Pipe A can fill a cistern in 12 hours and Pipe B can fill it in 18 hours. If both pipes are opened together, after how many hours should Pipe B be closed so that the cistern is full in 8 hours?",
    "options": [
      "4 hours",
      "5 hours",
      "6 hours",
      "7 hours",
      "8 hours"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": 2,
    "explanation": "LCM(12, 18) = 36 units. Rate A = 3 u/h, Rate B = 2 u/h. Pipe A runs for full 8 hours = 3 \u00d7 8 = 24 units. Remaining work = 36 - 24 = 12 units. Time for B = 12 / 2 = 6 hours.",
    "source_ref": "SBI Clerk Prelims 2016 Memory-Based Paper (Notification CRPD/CR/2016-17/04)",
    "source_url": "https://www.bankersadda.com/sbi-clerk-previous-year-question-paper/"
