    "passage": "The emergence of FinTech unicorns in India has radically redefined the retail consumer experience. Historically, securing an uncollateralized personal loan or credit card required an exhaustive paper trail, multiple physical visits to a bank branch, and weeks of bureaucratic manual verification. Today, open application programming interfaces (APIs), the Account Aggregator (AA) framework, and instant Aadhaar e-KYC have compressed loan sanctioning to under five minutes. Digital-first consumers can apply, receive underwriting approval, and disburse credit directly into their digital wallets from the comfort of their homes. However, instantaneous credit issuance has ignited concerns regarding reckless personal over-indebtedness, particularly among Gen Z and millennial borrowers. With 'Buy Now Pay Later' (BNPL) options seamlessly embedded into online checkouts, frictionless spending has decoupled consumer impulse from affordability. In response, the Reserve Bank of India issued digital lending guidelines mandating that loan disbursements must flow strictly from regulated commercial bank accounts to borrowers without intermediary pass-through accounts, and all fees must be transparently disclosed via a Key Fact Statement (KFS).",
